What are Security Token Offerings (STOs)?
Security Token Offerings represent a blockchain-powered fundraising mechanism where investors receive digital tokens backed by real-world assets, equity, or debt instruments. Unlike Initial Coin Offerings (ICOs) that primarily offer utility tokens, STOs operate within securities regulations - providing investor protections through asset-backed digital securities. These tokenized assets enable fractional ownership, enhanced liquidity through blockchain secondary markets, and automated compliance via smart contracts. Marketed as a compliant evolution of ICOs, STOs combine the efficiency of blockchain technology with the regulatory safeguards of traditional securities. Major financial hubs including the U.S., Singapore, and Switzerland have established regulatory frameworks for security tokens, creating defined compliance pathways that reduce legal uncertainty.

